  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">LAR GIBBON PROTECTION IN THAILAND&apos;S WESTERN FOREST COMPLEX</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to protect and potentially increase the population of lar gibbon in the Huai Kha Khaeng Wildlife Sanctuary (HKK). The improved patrol system in Thailand is called Smart Patrols and refers to a system of patrols that have the following characteristics: they are well-equipped with proper uniforms, high-quality field gear and good rations; they are well trained in physical fitness, ways to handle arrests and other encounters in the field and Thai law around ranger patrols; they collect data on threats, patrol routes and wildlife in a systematic fashion (using software such as MIST and its successor SMART-Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) and use this information in an adaptive management framework; patrolling happens at a high density over time and geographic space to ensure both deterrence, detection and capacity to respond to threats. Project objects are to, (1) maintain the Smart patrol system in Huai Kha Khaeng to the current intensity and coverage, and (2) implement a gibbon monitoring system in HKK where threats have been recorded</narrative>
  </description>
